node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence: an XFS logical volume was mounted at /srv/data, grown online to 2 GiB without changing its mount instance, and retained its pre-growth contents. The provider-wide restart protocol was also complete: a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, and recovered service, mount, storage, and data were captured and corroborated by lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["Package-manager consistency checks timed out both before and after execution, so the health impact of the CentOS-sourced LVM/device-mapper package installation on RHEL could not be independently assessed.","Lifecycle snapshots provide only bounded inventories; they confirm the two retained /tmp artifacts, unchanged listening services, and absence of failed units, but do not inventory every possible filesystem or configuration change."]}
